VERDICT: ANSWERED (8 flags) -- `acc 30 rd` and six `"1"`-count rows are omitted from the stall disclosure, `P:15-35` misstates the 10/33 red count, cell count, clause (b), and later-section updates, and `LEGS.out` carries pre-edit MD5s and `567s` vs `B:68`'s `568 s`.

FLAG: `B:17`, `B:70-75`, `B:319-321` vs `P:360-363` -- The stall disclosure claims that among rows wanting `alive` or `no`, only the two read sessions (`kill 20 rd`, `kill 28 rd`) and `tick 49` lack a companion `yes` announce row and read a stalled session green (twice and once, respectively)[cite: 1]. In `P:360-361`, `acc 30 rd` runs its own session `t, alive = session(guest_load(A_ISR))` and scores `("alive" if alive else "died")` against `want="alive"` with no companion row and no `printed(t, "v0")` check, so a stalled `acc 30 rd` session also reads green alone[cite: 2].
FLAG: `B:17`, `B:70-75`, `B:319-321` vs `P:244-269`, `P:604-605`, `P:668-670`, `P:677-678`, `P:684-686`, `P:710-713` -- The stall disclosure claims only rows wanting `alive` or `no` read a stall green[cite: 1]. Six rows wanting `"1"` (`latch 1x` at `P:604-605`, `latch 28wr` and `latch 30wr` at `P:668-670`, `latch tick` at `P:677-678`, `xbit rev` at `P:684-686`, and `xbit rev2` at `P:710-713`) score `str(counted(t, ...)) if alive else "died"` across two announce-producing events[cite: 2]; if a session stalls after the first access/tick announces (`counted == 1`) and before the second access or second tick at `step 65536` runs (note `P:244-269`: `session()` reads `fd` for only `0.35 + 2.5 = 2.85 s` after sending the last command and never reads `fd` during the 12 s `waitpid` poll), `alive` is `True` and `counted` is `"1"`, reading a broken latch green[cite: 2].
FLAG: `P:31-32`, `B:237-238` vs `P:11`, `P:43`, `B:382`, `B:399-432` -- Bullet 5 of the correction note states `"the pre-fix red is no longer '13 rows': on this instrument the pre-fix build scores 10/33"`[cite: 1, 2]. In `P:43` (`(the pre-fix red, 13 rows)`), `13` was the count of **red (`FAIL`) rows** on the 21-row instrument (`21 - 8 = 13` red rows when pre-fix scored `8/21`, `P:11`)[cite: 2]. On the 33-row instrument, `10/33` (`B:382`) means 10 green (`ok`) rows and **23 red (`FAIL`) rows** (`B:399-432`), with 2 of those 10 green rows (`kill 20 rd txt` and `kill 28 rd txt`, `B:407, 409`) scoring `got=no want=no` only because their sessions aborted (`got=DEAD`, `B:406, 408`)[cite: 1].
FLAG: `P:31-32`, `P:38-39`, `P:43`, `B:221-241` vs `B:24`, `B:297-298`, `B:359-360`, `B:379` -- `P:43` claims the detector catches `"reinstating any of the four abort() calls (the pre-fix red, 13 rows)"` and `P:38-39` claims every CATCH below has a measured kill in `killtable{,2}_20260917/`[cite: 2]. Per `B:24` (`G4`), `B:297-298`, and `B:359-360`, reinstating `abort()` individually at each fixed site of the fixed file is clause (b) and was not measured in `#566` (`B:379` reverted `dev_sgi_ip30.c` to `686d179c^` with all four `abort()` calls together, which is clause (a)), yet `P:15-35` (`B:221-241`) leaves `"reinstating any of the four abort() calls"` in `P:43` unqualified[cite: 1, 2].
FLAG: `P:16-17`, `B:222-223`, `B:329-330` vs `P:39`, `P:109`, `P:130`, `P:466`, `P:521`, `P:620`, `P:634`, `P:645-651` -- `P:16-17` (`B:222-223`) claims `"The file's later sections were updated and this one was not"` and `"five statements below are no longer true"`, and `B:329-330` claims `"the file's own later sections record the finished 33-row closure"`[cite: 1, 2]. Inside the CONTRACT (`P:37-152`), `P:39` (all catches measured in `killtable{,2}_20260917/`), `P:109` (`"All FIVE ISR sites print ONE IDENTICAL STRING"` -- only three ISR sites announce after F13 silenced the two read arms, `P:18-20`), and `P:130` (names row 4 `` `kill 30 rd' `` instead of `` `acc 30 rd' ``, `P:361`) are also untrue[cite: 2]; in the file's later sections (`P:153-743`), `P:466` (`"ALL FIVE ISR announces"`), `P:521` (`"all five ISR sites"`), `P:620` (`"The two READ arms ... both announce"`), and `P:634` (`` `kill 28 rd txt' stays GREEN under that mutant (the announce still fires) ``) were never updated after F13, and `P:645-651` (`THE LATCH-AXIS CLASS CLOSURE`) still records the **32-row** closure (`ALREADY CLOSED (6): ... and the TICK->ISR collision (xbit). CLOSED HERE (4): ...`) before `xbit rev2` (`P:692-718`) was added as row 33[cite: 2].
FLAG: `P:23-30`, `B:229-236` vs `P:50-53`, `P:77`, `P:573-587`, `P:645-718` -- Bullet 3 (`P:23-24`, `B:229-230`) repeats `P:645`'s `{4 announce sites} x {announce fires, latch sets} + {2 collision directions} = TEN cells, all rowed`, which was the 32-row count (`P:650-651`) that treated `xbit` (`xbit isr`/`xbit tick`, closing bit-collapse `M6`, `P:50-51, 573`) and `xbit rev` (`MA_assign20wr`, `P:683`) as the two collision directions before `V2_assigntick` (`MD_assigntick`) scored `32/32` (`P:692-693`) and required adding a 33rd row (`xbit rev2`, `P:710-718`, giving 11 latch-axis cells across 12 rows)[cite: 1, 2]. In Bullet 4 (`P:25-30`, `B:231-236`), `P:29-30` states `"MF's cell, a latch set on the 0x10028 READ, no longer exists: that arm no longer announces"`, omitting that `M9`'s cell at `P:52-53` (`0x10020-READ` latch set) also no longer exists for the same reason, while `latch 1x` (`P:25, 604-605`) now closes `MB` (`0x10020-WR`, `P:77`), `latch 28wr` (`P:668`) closes `0x10028-WR`, and `latch 30wr` (`P:668`) closes `MG` (`0x10030-WR`, `P:77`)[cite: 1, 2].
