### Q2. Controls on a broken run and exactness of the stall disclosure (including Angle 2)

* **Every `session()` call in `P` under a stall (Angle 2)**:
  * **Complete stall before any stepped access runs** (`alive == True` after the 12 s poll Kills the child at `P:254-269`, `t` has no `ISRMSG`/`TICKMSG` and no post-step `print v0`):
    * **10 rows across 8 sessions** want `"alive"` or `"no"`:
      * `acc 30 rd` (`P:360-361`, wants `"alive"`): **reads GREEN alone** (1 row; omitted by `B:17`, `B:70-75`, `B:319-321`)[cite: 1, 2].
      * `kill 20 rd` (`P:442-443`, wants `"alive"`) + `kill 20 rd txt` (`P:454`, wants `"no"`): **reads GREEN twice** (2 rows)[cite: 1, 2].
      * `kill 28 rd` (`P:442-443`, wants `"alive"`) + `kill 28 rd txt` (`P:454`, wants `"no"`): **reads GREEN twice** (2 rows)[cite: 1, 2].
      * `tick 49` (`P:505-506`, wants `"no"`): **reads GREEN alone** (1 row)[cite: 1, 2].
      * `kill 30 wr` (`P:458-459`), `tick 50` (`P:492-493`), `kill 20 wr` (`P:515-516`), `kill 28 wr` (`P:515-516`): their survival rows want `"alive"` and read green, while their companion `txt` rows (`kill 30 txt` at `P:469`, `tick 50 txt` at `P:499`, `kill 20 wr txt` at `P:524`, `kill 28 wr txt` at `P:524`) want `"yes"` and red[cite: 1, 2].
    * All `printed(t, "v0")` / `printed_last(t, "v0")` rows (`live` at `P:339-342`, `devsig` at `P:346-348`, `acc 18` at `P:355-356`, `acc 20000` at `P:386-393`, `acc 30000` at `P:398-399`, `acc imask` at `P:426-427`, `isr keep` at `P:533-536`, `isr clr` at `P:548-551`, `isr drop 30` at `P:559-562`, `isr 20 rd val` at `P:611-612`, `isr 28 rd val` at `P:629-630`) red on a stall before `step` runs because `v0` is preset to `SENTINEL = 0x5a5a5a5a` (`P:173, 290, 303`) or `"ABSENT"`, which differs from every row's `want` (including `"0x0"` for `isr 20/28 rd val`)[cite: 2].
  * **Mid-session stall before the second stepped access or second tick (`step 65536`) runs**:
    * `latch 1x` (`P:604-605`), `latch 28wr` (`P:668-670`), `latch 30wr` (`P:668-670`), `latch tick` (`P:677-678`), `xbit rev` (`P:684-686`), and `xbit rev2` (`P:710-713`) all want `"1"` from `str(counted(t, ...)) if alive else "died"`[cite: 2]. If the first store/tick announces (`counted == 1`) and the second store or `step 65536` stalls beyond `rd(0.35)` + `rd(2.5)` (`P:244-245`, since `P:254-269` never reads `fd` during the 12 s poll), `alive` is `True` and `counted` is `"1"`, so **all six rows read a stall green** on a build with a defeated/clobbered latch[cite: 2].
* **Scoring controls (`B:84-124`)**:
  * The shell scoring block itself requires unique `IP30ABORT_RESULT=`, `IP30ABORT_CONTROL=OK`, `IP30ABORT_DONE`, exit status `0`, all 33 named `ok` rows, and `33/33/33/33/0` counts (`B:86-124`)[cite: 1]. However, in `selftest/SELFTEST.out`, `n3_rowdup` (`B:442-443`) replaced `tick 49` with `tick 50` instead of adding a 34th line, and no selftest case tests `IP30ABORT_RESULT=32/33` with 33 `ok` rows (`n1_onefail` at `B:438-439` and `n8_contra` at `B:452-453` both test 1 `FAIL` row with `IP30ABORT_RESULT=33/33`)[cite: 1].

### Q3. Ruling on D1 and D2

* **D1 (`B:34-37` -- keep `ip30abortkill` open vs. close now)**: **Keep open (`separate`) holds**[cite: 1].
  * *Why separate holds*: Closing `ip30abortkill` requires moving the two disclosed escapes (`V7_nocounter` at 32/32 and `V8_len4` at 33/33, `P:33, 79-96`) onto a surviving carrier row, replacing the 21-row witness pair (`8/21 -> 21/21`) in the ledger witness field with the 33-row pair (`10/33 -> 33/33`), and settling clause (b) (`B:293-298, 357-360`)[cite: 1, 2].
  * *Harder on the adopted position*: `B:297-298` and `B:359-360` assert flatly that *"no kill table holds such a mutant"* for clause (b), whereas `P:479-480` (`M_tick_abort (which is ALSO clause (b) at site 4 -- a VERBATIM REINSTATEMENT the probe could not see)`) and `P:512-513` (`M_wf20_abort_wr and M_wf28_abort_wr -- abort() kept INSIDE the write arm`) explicitly name single-site `abort()` mutants in `#531`[cite: 1, 2]. Check `regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/opus_killtable_20260917/mutate*.py` (`X:33-48`) before writing that no kill table holds them[cite: 2].
* **D2 (`B:38-41` -- edit `ip30_abort_probe.py` docstring in this commit vs. leave unmodified)**: **Editing the docstring holds in principle, but `2c` (`P:14-35`) is broken as written**[cite: 1, 2].
  * *Why editing holds in principle*: `gate_arm.sh` (`B:64-65`) explicitly directs readers to `"The probe's CONTRACT, its MEASURED ESCAPES and its DOES NOT CATCH list are in its header"`[cite: 1]; leaving the header claiming `"THE CLOSURE IS OWED"` and `"SIX announce sites"` (`P:44, 59-62, 84`) makes the new gate comment cite a false record[cite: 2].
  * *Harder on the adopted position*: (1) `P:16-17` falsely claims later sections were updated and only five statements below are untrue (`P:39, 43, 109, 130, 466, 521, 620, 634, 645-651` are also stale)[cite: 2]; (2) `P:31-32` conflates `13` red rows with `10/33` (which is **23 red rows**, `B:399-432`)[cite: 1, 2]; (3) `P:23-24` repeats the 32-row 10-cell count before `xbit rev2` (`P:692-718`)[cite: 2]; and (4) editing `ip30_abort_probe.py` after `LEGS566` ran made `probe md5 5bf04f2de35af34d517bd286499d5b98` in `legs/LEGS.out` (`B:369`) stale[cite: 1].

### Q4. Anything else owed in this commit, and which dispositions in Section 0 are wrong

* **What else is owed before commit**:
  1. **Reset and rebuild `/tmp/gx566` before the gate 14 run (`B:44-45` vs `B:379-381, 393`)**: Using a clean HEAD binary from `/tmp/gx566` as `PMAX` (rather than `build/gxemul`, which carries another session's uncommitted sources, `B:44, 336-337`) is the right binary choice, **but** `LEGS566` left `/tmp/gx566` on the **pre-fix** mutant (`dev_sgi_ip30.c := 686d179c^`, built at `11:18:35`, `B:379-381`) with `.MUTANT` (`B:393`)[cite: 1]. You must reset `src/devices/dev_sgi_ip30.c` to HEAD, remove `.MUTANT`, and rebuild `/tmp/gx566` before running gate 14[cite: 1].
  2. **Refresh `legs/LEGS.out` MD5s (`B:369`)**: Re-record or re-run after fixing `2a` (`gate_arm.sh`) and `2c` (`ip30_abort_probe.py`) so `LEGS.out`'s `probe md5` and `gate_arm.sh md5` match the committed files[cite: 1].
  3. **Ledger `state_note` rows (`B:282, 496`)**: `2e` (`B:268-299`) adds prose bullets to `OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md`, but shows no diff to the ledger table `state_note` rows for `wiringcliff` and `ip30abortkill` (whether those live in `OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md` or a separate ledger file is **UNSETTLED** without the full `OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md`)[cite: 1].
* **Which accepted dispositions in Section 0 (`B:14-32`) are wrong**:
  * **`A2` (`B:17`) is WRONG**: It states that among rows wanting `alive` or `no`, only the two read sessions read a stall green twice and `tick 49` once, omitting `acc 30 rd` (`P:360-361`, which wants `"alive"` and reads a stalled session green alone) and omitting mid-session stalls on the six count rows wanting `"1"` (`latch 1x`, `latch 28wr`, `latch 30wr`, `latch tick`, `xbit rev`, `xbit rev2`, `P:604-605, 668-686, 710-713`)[cite: 1, 2].
  * **`A1` (`B:16`) is DEFECTIVE in `2c` (`B:220-241`, `P:14-35`)**: The added note falsely claims `P`'s later sections were updated and only five statements below are untrue (`P:16-17`), repeats the 32-row 10-cell count (`P:23-24`), and conflates 13 red rows with `10/33` (23 red rows, `P:31-32`)[cite: 1, 2].
  * **`G4` (`B:24`) is INCOMPLETE in `2c` (`P:31-32, 43`)**: `B:24` says clause (a) vs. (b) was relabelled, but `P:43` (`reinstating any of the four abort() calls`) was left unqualified by `P:15-35`, and whether `#531` measured single-site `abort()` mutants (`M_tick_abort`, `M_wf20_abort_wr`, `M_wf28_abort_wr` named at `P:479-480, 512-513`) is **UNSETTLED** without `regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/opus_killtable_20260917/mutate*.py`[cite: 1, 2].

